# Live blackboard + logs are generated; schema.sql + migrations are the source of truth.
store/*.db
store/*.db-wal
store/*.db-shm
# db-restore's own "move aside, never delete" sidecars (orchestrator/db_restore.py) —
# timestamped .bak-*/.failed-* siblings it leaves next to store/blackboard.db.
store/*.db.bak-*
store/*.db.bak-*-wal
store/*.db.bak-*-shm
store/*.db.failed-*
logs/runs/
logs/*.log
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
# candidate specs are generated by the proposer; keep the dir, not the churn
specs/candidates/*.yaml
# transient mining output (vet -> promote into working/ or held-out/)
scenarios/staging/*.yaml
# transient researcher output (vet -> feed the proposer)
research/staging/*.yaml
# generated executive summaries (the daily 09:00 update); keep the dir, not the churn
updates/*.md
# generated blog posts (the factory's accessible write-ups); keep the dir, not the churn
blog/*.md
# the factory's own development diary (narrative entries + raw events) — local only
.dev-diary/
# runtime control artifacts — kill-switch, live mode flag, supervisor lock, generated dashboard snapshot — local only
STOP
.factory-mode
.autopilot.pid*
logs/fleet.html
# F9 (round-2 integration fix, publication-broker security review): the dev/single-user
# broker spool default (common/paths.py: FACTORY_BROKER_SPOOL unset -> <factory>/state/
# broker) lives INSIDE this checkout. In armed dev/single-user mode the factory writes
# publication envelopes, receipts, and a full bare git repo there — without this line,
# `git add -A` commits them into the PUBLIC factory repo and `git clean -fdx` deletes
# unprocessed envelopes out from under an in-flight publication. Production deployments
# point FACTORY_BROKER_SPOOL/autonomy.broker_spool_root at /Users/Shared/factory-broker
# instead (outside any checkout), but the default must be safe too.
state/
